hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2867","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adiyy and Muhammad ibn Ja'far and 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid, from 'Awf ibn Abi Jamīlah, from Ziyād ibn Ḥaṣīn, who narrated to us Abū al-'Āliyah, who said:

Ibn 'Abbās (RA) told me that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said on the morning of the Day of 'Aqabah:

Ibn Abi 'Adiyy mentioned in his narration, and likewise 'Awf said:

""Bring me some pebbles,"" which are the pebbles used for throwing (ramy). When they were placed in his hand, he (ﷺ) said:

""With such as these, with such as these. Beware of going to extremes in religion, for those who came before you were destroyed only by going to extremes in religion.""

**CHAPTER:**"
"2868","Bundar narrated it to us another time with the same wording, except that he said: Ziyad ibn Husayn narrated to me. And Bundar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: 'Awf narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Husayn narrated to us: Abu al-'Aliyah narrated to me, he said: Ibn 'Abbas said to me - 'Awf said: I do not know whether it was al-Fadl or 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas - he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the morning of al-'Aqabah: ""Pick up for me some pebbles,"" with the same wording exactly."
